ser":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T11:11:47-07:00","id":1139736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1139375-mage-the-ascension-revised-metaplot-references?p=1139456#post1139456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. I thought /somewhere/ along those events, the ending of the Changling gameline was also explained in-world. I must be misremembering.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, none of it ended the Changeling line, BUUUUUUUUT, they didn't publish very much for the line after that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T14:52:55-07:00","id":1139779,"title":"","content":"I just thought Changeling just unceremoniously ended. They did the winter stuff, but apart from that just dropped it fairly unceremoniously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T09:34:36-07:00","id":1139953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1139375-mage-the-ascension-revised-metaplot-references?p=1139779#post1139779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just thought Changeling just unceremoniously ended. They did the winter stuff, but apart from that just dropped it fairly unceremoniously.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's basically what happened. They stopped publishing books for it. They rounded everything up in the Big Book of Endings (aka Time of Judgement) along with all the other dangling lines.<br /> <br /> On the bright side, less to backtrack on for C20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T23:29:55-07:00","id":1140100,"title":"","content":"Oh, a random note, Nico;<br /> I was looking for more material on Mage metaplot, and I found out that in &quot;Tales of Magick: Dark Adventure&quot; There is a whole chapter about the Mage Metaplot events between 2nd and Revised, including the Concordia War. You might wanna peek at that book.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> To list, it contains plot info and story hook options for<br /> * The Concordia War<br /> * The War Of Ruins on Mars and Mars' umbralscape after the fall of Doissetep<br /> * Project Invictus' N.W.O. sponsored covert op against SPD.<br /> * The hunt for Voormas' floating Chantry of Helekar<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 09-14-2017, 04:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T09:16:00-07:00","id":1140199,"title":"","content":"Didn't Helekar's Chantry reveal itself to be some kind of necro-kaiju and get up and run off?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 09-14-2017, 07:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T09:26:32-07:00","id":1140203,"title":"","content":"I thank you very much. With all that info, I'll decide what I'll do. I fear that playing both events (Horizon War and Avatar Storm) will be perceived as two failures by my players, which can be a lot to take on.<br /> <br /> My idea was to merge both events saying that the bomb was launched on Concordia to destroy the Ascension Warrior semigod. I'm still poundering ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T10:25:22-07:00","id":1140225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1139375-mage-the-ascension-revised-metaplot-references?p=1140203#post1140203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thank you very much. With all that info, I'll decide what I'll do. I fear that playing both events (Horizon War and Avatar Storm) will be perceived as two failures by my players, which can be a lot to take on.<br /> <br /> My idea was to merge both events saying that the bomb was launched on Concordia to destroy the Ascension Warrior semigod. I'm still poundering ^^</div> </div> </div> </div>Or you could do the opposite: Your players may be very capable but they probably can't be everywhere at once (well, not without Correspondence 4/Spirit 3-5, and even that may have downsides).<br /> <br /> *Generating the Storn as the result of many seemingly unconected events would provide you with enough leeway to make it happen even if the players succeed at stoping one or two of them (you could, perhaps, reward them by reducing the intensity of the Storm a little or allowing a few Masters to escape)<br /> <br /> *If the Ascencion Warrior isn't omnipotent but has many alies and a lot of schemes going on, the War will be on several fronts (at least Doissetep and Concordia, fell free to include more) and the main consequences of the event may happen even if the players manage to kill the demigod.<br /> <br /> Even if you manage to, say, impede Concordia fall: the explosion of Doissetep combined with the damage of the attack and the Storm first winds (that affected allt he Umbra) may still force everyone to flee the Realm, and a lot of Masters, if not all of them, will die as consequence. Why players didn't stop the Storm?, because they were busy stopping a demigod. That way your players are free to do what they can, but they probably can't do everything and may have to choose what to save. If everything goes to hell, your players may regard a few victories as the best that could have happened. That's very different, I think, from failing to stop a wizard because he has Plot Armor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 09-14-2017, 02:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T12:01:49-07:00","id":1140266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1139375-mage-the-ascension-revised-metaplot-references?p=1140199#post1140199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't Helekar's Chanrty reveal itself to be some kind of necro-kaiju and get up and run off?</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds amazing, scary, crazy, and I want to subscribe to its newsletter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T12:02:11-07:00","id":1140267,"title":"","content":"If you're worried about the actual path you want to take seeming too dark or like too much of a failure, just allow for it to have been worse. The invasion of Horizon was supposed to allow the Technocracy to follow its links to the many individual horizon realms held by the Traditions and let them exterminate their Umbral presence once and for all, and instead your PCs manage to sever the links to Horizon, giving the Technocracy a Pyrrhic victory. Or perhaps the Avatar Storm would have pushed through the Gauntlet and shredded all Awakened on Earth, but for your plucky PCs somehow reinforcing the Gauntlet worldwide.<br /> <br /> And yes, the House of Helekar runs around and punches the PCs during the &quot;canonical&quot; ending in the Time of Judgment. Also in that scenario you have to beat up pretas which are the jhor leaking out of Voormas. And the guy who manages to kill Voormas gets his jhor and drive to end the cycle. <br /> <br /> I didn't really like that ending.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T09:37:45-07:00","id":1141436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1139375-mage-the-ascension-revised-metaplot-references?p=1140225#post1140225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or you could do the opposite: Your players may be very capable but they probably can't be everywhere at once (well, not without Correspondence 4/Spirit 3-5, and even that may have downsides).<br /> <br /> *Generating the Storn as the result of many seemingly unconected events would provide you with enough leeway to make it happen even if the players succeed at stoping one or two of them (you could, perhaps, reward them by reducing the intensity of the Storm a little or allowing a few Masters to escape)<br /> <br /> *If the Ascencion Warrior isn't omnipotent but has many alies and a lot of schemes going on, the War will be on several fronts (at least Doissetep and Concordia, fell free to include more) and the main consequences of the event may happen even if the players manage to kill the demigod.<br /> <br /> Even if you manage to, say, impede Concordia fall: the explosion of Doissetep combined with the damage of the attack and the Storm first winds (that affected allt he Umbra) may still force everyone to flee the Realm, and a lot of Masters, if not all of them, will die as consequence. Why players didn't stop the Storm?, because they were busy stopping a demigod. That way your players are free to do what they can, but they probably can't do everything and may have to choose what to save. If everything goes to hell, your players may regard a few victories as the best that could have happened. That's very different, I think, from failing to stop a wizard because he has Plot Armor.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I get what you mean. Actually, in the final battle on Horizon, I was going to let them choose what to save, what to fight and what to let behind. The reward would be the political influence they would get, being some of the few experimented Mages left after the disappearance of the Masters. The core of my campaign is after the Horizon War when there is few things left and everything is to be built again. How the Storm fit into that ? Not sure anymore... May be you're right. Both events could happen the same period and they were not aware of the awakening of Zapathusera.<br /> <br /> The possibility is to let them play this second plot and put them in the situation in which they have to choose to stop the bomb or let it explode to destroy the Antedeluvian. If they choose to stop it though, may be I will reright the plot to avoid the Storm and I will play a kind of Mages against Vampires Blood War. Not sure...<br /> <br /> For now, they do not even know the Ascension Warrior is free. They're occupied ploting in Horizon ^^<br /> They currently fight over the case of a poor guy accused of Infernalism. The trial is sham with several factions wanting the guy to be innocent or guilty because of political influence Whatever the truth is is secondary for these factions since they care only about their positions and the implications of such a trial.<br /> <br /> I intend to use the result of the trial to draw the alliances and feuds between the different factions and the players. Everything they do now will impact the political landscape during the Horizon War. Thus, I still have time to decide what to do with the Avatar Storm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T09:44:23-07:00","id":1141440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1139375-mage-the-ascension-revised-metaplot-references?p=1140267#post1140267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're worried about the actual path you want to take seeming too dark or like too much of a failure, just allow for it to have been worse. The invasion of Horizon was supposed to allow the Technocracy to follow its links to the many individual horizon realms held by the Traditions and let them exterminate their Umbral presence once and for all, and instead your PCs manage to sever the links to Horizon, giving the Technocracy a Pyrrhic victory. Or perhaps the Avatar Storm would have pushed through the Gauntlet and shredded all Awakened on Earth, but for your plucky PCs somehow reinforcing the Gauntlet worldwide.<br /> <br /> And yes, the House of Helekar runs around and punches the PCs during the &quot;canonical&quot; ending in the Time of Judgment. Also in that scenario you have to beat up pretas which are the jhor leaking out of Voormas. And the guy who manages to kill Voormas gets his jhor and drive to end the cycle.<br /> <br /> I didn't really like that ending.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that is another option I'm considering, that is making the Avatar Storm much more a threat than it actually is (which is huge enough in the first place) to make the players victory a grey one.<br /> <br /> I actually intend to play the Ascension scenario with Voormas (the first one of the four of the Time of Judgement book). However, I intend to change the end to avoid destroying everything or saving everything in the end. I do not want the WoD to have an ending that way (I prefer the Storm-came-then-left-at-some-point possibility). I'm to afraid of being myself disappointed by the end. Reaching that end could be a final point to myself playing Mage, which I'm clearly not prepared to !!!! (I had that friend who stopped playing Vampire after having played a Gehenna scenario because of the feeling of closure got in the end). Not sure if it's clear ^^<br /> <br /> Well anyway, the objective is to close that part of the metaplot to imagine a different world, more modern of the WoD. Something adapted to 2017 you know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T03:06:57-07:00","id":1142444,"title":"","content":"The Revised Convention Books tweaked the Revised setting considerably to allow for the fact that they were published a decade after the Time of Judgment. In particular, the VE book implies that the Avatar Storm had more to do with the fall of the various Horizon Realms than with the Week of Nightmares, though the latter served as the final straw and triggered the physical destruction of the remaining Horizon Realms that hadn't already fallen. Think of the 2e metaplot as turning the Horizon Realms into a house of cards, and the Week of Nightmares as the push that finally knocked it down. (There's also something about a Euthanatos Node in India being the only remaining reliable connection to the Umbra; but whether that's because of the Week of Nightmares or something Helekar did \u2014 or both \u2014 is an open question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T13:30:57-07:00","id":1142673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1139375-mage-the-ascension-revised-metaplot-references?p=1142444#post1142444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also something about a Euthanatos Node in India being the only remaining reliable connection to the Umbra; but whether that's because of the Week of Nightmares or something Helekar did \u2014 or both \u2014 is an open question.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that was a hole ripped in reality at the spot where the Ravnos antediluvian died...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}